      "writtenOn": "2021-04-27T16:44:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This seems reasonable to me, but I\u0027m concerned about the growing number of bindings we\u0027re adding that aren\u0027t actual drivers. Would it be possible for us to move cbi_ssfc.h to zephyr/include/drivers/ and cbi_ssfc.c to zephyr/drivers/?\n\nWe would then create an API for the driver that would create the mapping and not have to expose the motion_sensors_alt array from the motionsense_sensors.c. The hook would be declared there and will pass the 2 arrays to create the mapping.\n\nThe other up side to this is that the driver will not use the hard coded DT_PATH and will be a bit more flexible.",
      "revId": "deb82de76c202bc7e2d8e02d7624c46bfa862b44",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
